------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE drums.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  3022					      include	"drums.asm"
      1  3022							; Fat Chip 64 - drums on the MidiNES
      2  3022							;
      3  3022							; Two sources, one kit:
      4  3022							;   the keytar's rhythm   MIDI in channel 16 (Yamaha SHS-10: 45 kick, 48 tom,
      5  3022							;			   52 snare, 57 hat, 62 cymbal; velocity 127 = accent,
      6  3022							;			   64 = hit, 56 = ghost)
      7  3022							;   the beat demos	   G picks one of six Beat Lab beats (and its kit),
      8  3022							;			   RETURN starts / stops it, at its own tempo (B taps
      9  3022							;			   a new one)
     10  3022							; Kick, snare, toms and percussion are samples on the MidiNES's sample
     11  3022							; channel (one at a time: a hit within DRUM_WINDOW ms of a more important one
     12  3022							; is dropped; kick > snare > tom > perc). Hats and cymbals are NES noise:
     13  3022							; a note-on, then a note-off after the sound's length, the level set with
     14  3022							; CC7; closed hats vary their note and level a little on each hit (the Beat
     15  3022							; Lab's noise hats). Kits are in beats.asm (tools/gen_beats.py).
